※ The separator is what says which kind of type is being defined, so a
※ definition using both would be saying two things about itself, and there is
※ no type that is both.

type Confused = a : u8 ; b : u8 | c : u8

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
